      "title": "[Direct Closed Mail and Parcel Mail Services Inaugurated or Resumed during the Fiscal Year]",
      "caption_extra": "Post Office — Postal Union: Exchange services. \"The following inauguration or resumption of direct closed mail or parcel mail services took place during the fiscal year\" (the 24th fiscal year, ending June 30, 1936).",
      "parts": [
        {
          "label": null,
          "columns": [
            "Item"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Direct exchange of parcels was inaugurated between China and Spain with effect from July 1, 1935"
            ],
            [
              "An insured box service was introduced between China and Netherlands Indies from February 15, 1936"
            ],
            [
              "Direct exchange of closed mails between Ierhkoszetang and the U.S.S.R. resumed"
            ],
            [
              "Direct closed parcel mails were:"
            ],
            [
              "despatched from Brindisi transiti, Genova Porto, and Trieste for Shanghai"
            ],
            [
              "forwarded from Sarawak and Sandakan for Swatow"
            ],
            [
              "despatched from Auckland, Wellington, Mauritius, Bangkok, Durban, Suva, Dublin, Negapatan, and Madura for Shanghai and Canton"
            ],
            [
              "sent from Praha 7 Cizina for Tientsin"
            ],
            [
              "despatched from Aden, Buenos Aires, Beira, and Lourenço Marques for Shanghai"
            ],
            [
              "despatched from Sandakan, Colombo, Bale 2, Menado, Calgary, and Vancouver Railway for Canton"
            ],
            [
              "forwarded from Geneva 2 for Shanghai via Marseilles"
            ],
            [
              "made up by Tandjongpriok for Canton and Minhow (Foochow)"
            ],
            [
              "made up by Bruxelles I for Peiping and Tientsin"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ],
      "transcriber_notes": [
